data.content:
`SafeAreaEdges` alone doesn't guarantee edge-to-edge rendering. You likely need two additional things:

**1. iOS — disable safe area insets on the page:**

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns:ios="clr-namespace:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.PlatformConfiguration.iOSSpecific;assembly=Microsoft.Maui.Controls"
             ios:Page.UseSafeArea="False">
    <Image Source="photo.jpg" Aspect="AspectFill"
           VerticalOptions="Fill" HorizontalOptions="Fill" />
</ContentPage>
```

**2. Android — opt into edge-to-edge (draw behind system bars):**

In `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    // Draw behind status bar and navigation bar
    AndroidX.Core.View.WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window, false);

    // Make system bars transparent
    Window.SetStatusBarColor(Android.Graphics.Color.Transparent);
    Window.SetNavigationBarColor(Android.Graphics.Color.Transparent);
}
```

> **Note:** On Android 15+ (API 35), edge-to-edge is enforced by default, but on older targets you must opt in explicitly as shown above.

**Summary of what was missing:** iOS needs `UseSafeArea="False"`, and Android needs `SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window, false)` plus transparent system bar colors. Without the Android platform code, the system bars reserve space regardless of your XAML settings.
